G-5: send offsite backups to an S3-compatible endpoint (Hetzner Object Storage).

Agent commit: 1956afb39613aafc88d821a9b1762ae397d4f588
Agent repository: https://github.com/frappe/agent
License: AGPL-3.0 (derived from Agent code)

Press sends ENDPOINT_URL in the offsite auth (press/agent.py,
_get_offsite_backup_config, Press v0.154.1). Unpatched Agent ignores it: the
boto3 uploads go to AWS, and the streaming rclone path fixes the endpoint to
s3.<region>.amazonaws.com. This patch adds agent/offsite_s3.py. Every offsite
S3 client (site backups, binlogs, audit logs) now takes its settings from it.
With ENDPOINT_URL set, boto3 gets endpoint_url and rclone gets
--s3-provider Other and --s3-endpoint. Without it, behaviour is unchanged.
Credentials still reach rclone only through the environment.

Remove when: Agent upstream reads ENDPOINT_URL for offsite uploads. Then move
the pinned Agent commit forward and delete this patch.
Test: backend/deploy/tests/test_agent_patches.py

